te on their own walt takes the  street name heisenberg and jesse  recruits his goofball stoner friends  badger skinny pete and combo to handle  sales of the three jessie is closest  with combo in a season 3 flashback scene  we even learned that the winnebago rb  that he and walt used to cook math  belong to combo's mother one morning  combo is working a street corner when a  black muscle car parks nearby with two  men inside watching him soon after a  young boy bicycles around the car honks  twice and before he knows what's  happened combo has been shot dead  combo's death directly leads walt to  seek out somewhat handle distribution of  his math which puts him in the sights of  the show's greatest antagonist chilean  chicken man gus fring jesse meanwhile  devastated by combo's death and hurt by  walt's all-business attitude slips  further into his addiction to heroin  artist and recovering drug addict jane  margulis is trying to piece her life  back together when she runs the other  side of her duplex to jesse in season  two as these things often go a somewhat  prickly business relationship warms into  a friendship and then to something more  but it's already a sad truth of the show  that no one can know walter jesse and  get away unscathed before long jesse and  jane's addictive personalities bring out  the worst in each other they also make  pie in the sky plans to get clean and  move to new zealand but first just one  more night of getting high waltz returns  later that night to make amends with  jessie and finds the two of them strung  out jane sleeping on her back begins to  throw up walt could roll her over but he  doesn't instead he watches jane choke to  death walt let jane die because he knew  her being with jesse would lead to his  eventual overdose one day and also  because she tried blackmailing him  threatening to expose his  drug-affiliated secrets jane was jesse's  last tether to a life outside of walt  the cartels and meth and his guilt  lingers for the remainder of the series  walt meanwhile feels little to no guilt  over jane's death and doesn't reveal his  role in her death to jessie until the  end of the series  i was there  and i watched her die but jesse was not  the only person to love jane and her  death has further consequences on a  massive scale the first episode of  season two teases a terrible future  event by depicting a mangled pink teddy  bear floating in the white family pool  the explanation when finally revealed in  the season two finale is unexpected yet  at the same time unavoidable a tragic  accident set in motion by every decision  walt and jessie ever made jane's death  hits jessie hard but it also devastates  her father donald an air traffic  controller who takes a few weeks off  from work in order to recover from his  grief when he finally returns to his  position at the albuquerque airport he  is shaky but ready to get back to his  routine at his council he guides  wayfarer flight 515 but his mind begins  to wander clear direct to albuquerque  via the  aircraft calling please stand by  suddenly wayfarer 515 collides with  another aircraft high above avq sending  bodies and debris flying all over the  city including straight into walt's  backyard a blunt but powerful metaphor  for the destruction he's brought upon  his family  months after jane's death jesse has  kicked his heroin habit and found a new  partner in young mom andrea contio  andrea looks after her young son brock  as well as her younger brother tomas who  is mixed up in gang activity but  albuquerque is a small town and jesse  soon makes a terrible discovery tomas is  the young boy who shot combo to death in  the street and the gang he is running  with is affiliated with gus fring jesse  goes to walt for help wanting to kill  the dealers using tomas but walt goes to  gus instead who calls a meeting and  declares that the gang is to no longer  use children in their business the  dealers agree and take gus's directions  literally by killing tomas now bent on  revenge for both andrea's brother and  combo jesse sets out to gun down the two  dealers and probably get himself killed  in the process as he's about to confront  them however walt plows his car into the  two kills one with a bullet to the head  and tells jesse  run  poor old gail bettiker gail is a gifted  chemist an all-around sweet guy a  karaoke fan and a man with the  incredible misfortune to be caught  between two of the coldest most paranoid  men alive walter white and gus fring  brought on as walt's assistant in the  french-built super lab in season three  gail and walt have a fruitful  partnership at first but walt grows  concerned that gail may be there as his  replacement rather than his assistant  and fabricates reasons to fire gail and  replace him with jesse after the deaths  of tomas and frank's two dealers jesse  goes into hiding what makes the deal to  forget about jesse and continue cooking  for gus with gail reluctantly returning  as his assistant this time walt's  paranoia is founded gus has indeed  brought gail back in order to take over  the super lab once walt and jesse have  been killed springs fixers mike and  victor take walt to the super lab to  kill him but not before walt calls jesse  who shows up at gayle's apartment with a  gun and shoots him at point blank range  the fifth episode of season five opens  on a young boy out in the desert alone  not much happens before the opening  credits roll and the boy isn't seen  again for nearly another hour after the  fiery death of gus spring at the end of  season four walt jesse and mike are now  their own bosses in the meth game with  all the responsibility that entails for  one they're dealing with gus's former  business partner at a german  conglomerate they have also hired a  young new assistant todd who is eager to  impress most importantly though they  need an industrial amount of methylamine  to continue production and the only way  to get it is to rob a freight train what  follows is a marvelously suspenseful  heist sequence as walt jesse and todd  conspired to bring the train to a halt  in the middle of the desert drain the  methylamine it's carrying replace it  with water and get out without getting  killed or caught it goes off of that  hitch and the three men are high off the  exhilaration that is until drew sharp  that young boy from the opening sequence  shows up again having witnessed  everything so without a second thought  todd pulls out a pistol and shoots him  dead  fan favorite character mike erman trout  was introduced at the end of season 2  with saul goodman's cleaner arriving at  jesse's apartment to take care of jane's  body and make sure nothing incriminating  is left in the house mike was soon  brought back as a recurring character in  seasons three and four an enforcer an  all-around bagman for gus spring by  season five he was business partners  with walt even in the company of  geniuses like gus and walt mike tends to  be the smartest guy in the room the  philly x-cop who's seen-it-all attitude  hides a deep moral code that moral code  is consistently offended however by  walter white many of the show's deaths  continue to weigh on him and mike  expresses an almost fatherly concern  toward jesse as he falls ever further  into walt's influence the money is good  so mike keeps working with him but  something's got to give that's something  finally does give when the dea catches  mike's lawyer distributing money to his  associates in prison paying for their  continued silence mike decides to skip  town but needs his emergency getaway bag  picked up from the airport walt delivers  it to him at some far away spot near a  creek and in their final conversation  mike lashes out blaming walt for ruining  the good deal they all had under gus  spring you just had to blow it up you  and your pride and your ego you just had  to be the man in a rage walt shoots mike  in the gut and this iconic character is  left to bleed out by the creek alpha  male dea agent hank schroeder loves his  family including his brother-in-law  walter white even if he and white don't  always understand each other introduced  in season one as a meathead jock gone to  seed hank bloomed over the course of the  series revealing hidden depths and  turning into someone the audience could  really root for by the season five's  mid-season finale in 2012 hank has  finally discovered that the drug  kingping heisenberg who he's been  hunting for nearly two years is in fact  his brother-in-law the rest of the  season concerns his fight to bring walt  to justice that struggle reaches a  terrible conclusion in the standout  episode ozymandias in the previous  episode hank and jesse team up and lure  walt out to the remote spot on a native  reservation where he has buried barrels  of cash hank slaps handcuffs on walt but  his triumph is short-lived as walt's new  business partners a gang of neo-nazis  led by todd's uncle jack show up as well  a shootout ensues that leaves hank  wounded walt tries to talk jack out of  killing hank but hank shuts him down  you're too stupid to see  he made up his mind 10 minutes ago jack  shoots him and walt's world finally  crumbles  of all of walter white's victims jesse  is arguably the one who suffers the most  he is put through the ringer in every  season and every time he tries to get  out walt's gravitational pull brings him  right back around for more punishment  the end of season 5 has jessie suffered  to an almost absurd degree as he is  kidnapped by todd and uncle jack after  hank's death and forced to cook math  walt meanwhile has fled to new hampshire  as the full ugly truth of his drug  empire comes to light if there's a  glimmer of hope in jessie's life though  it's the thought of seeing andrea and  brock again  todd knows this and in the series  penultimate episode he snuffs out half  of his hope after jesse tries to escape  and refuses to cook math he puts jesse  in the back of his truck and drives to  andrea's house todd knocks on the door  introduces himself to her as a friend of  jesse's and promptly shoots her in the  back of the head jesse screams in pain  and rage flailing trying to escape his  holds uncle jack sitting in the front  seat issues a chilling command  hey  remember you're still a kid  breaking bad really doesn't get much  more brutal than this check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  shows are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]

